meta {
  name: 9f. Toggle openDataAccess → true (triggers UPDATE saga)
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id/released/meta
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{sagaDataSetId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Saga Test DataSet",
    "description": "Dataset for end-to-end saga workflow test",
    "openDataAccess": true
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  // The CREATE saga (step 8) must have fully settled before we can update released meta,
  // otherwise the backend returns 409 (saga in-flight). Poll pendingSagaType until null.
  // assignments/namedApis are intentionally omitted from the body: per DataSetInputDTO the
  // null reconciler leaves those collections untouched (so step 10 assignments survive).
  // NOTE: Bruno's QuickJS sandbox lacks URLSearchParams and does not honour a validateStatus
  // function across the VM boundary, so we build the form body as a string and use try/catch.
  const axios = require('axios');
  const base = bru.getEnvVar('baseUrl');
  const kc = bru.getEnvVar('keycloakUrl');
  const realm = bru.getEnvVar('realm');
  const id = bru.getVar('sagaDataSetId');

  const form =
    'grant_type=password' +
    '&client_id=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('clientId')) +
    '&client_secret=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('clientSecret')) +
    '&username=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('username')) +
    '&password=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('password'));

  // Fail loudly if readiness can't be proven: without a token every poll below 401s, `pending`
  // never leaves its sentinel, and the loop would fall through as if the saga had settled —
  // sending the PUT into the 409 race this guard exists to remove.
  let bearer = '';
  try {
    const tok = await axios.post(`${kc}/realms/${realm}/protocol/openid-connect/token`, form, {
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
    });
    bearer = tok.data && tok.data.access_token;
  } catch (e) {
    throw new Error(`Settle-check token fetch failed: ${e.message}`);
  }
  if (!bearer) {
    throw new Error('Settle-check token fetch returned no access_token');
  }

  let settled = false;
  for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) {
    let pending = 'unknown'; // sentinel: a failed read stays "not settled", never breaks the loop
    try {
      const r = await axios.get(`${base}/datasets/${id}`, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${bearer}` } });
      pending = r.data.pendingSagaType;
    } catch (e) { /* transient; retry */ }
    if (pending === null || pending === undefined) { settled = true; break; }
    await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, 2000));
  }
  if (!settled) {
    throw new Error('Dataset did not settle (pendingSagaType still set) — refusing to update during an active saga');
  }
}

tests {
  test("openDataAccess update accepted (200)", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("Dataset now reports openDataAccess=true", function() {
    expect(res.body.openDataAccess).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 9f of 18** — Flip a released dataset to open data access (issue #1368, journey J3).

  `PUT /datasets/{id}/released/meta` with `openDataAccess: true` updates the released dataset and **persists** the flag. The route is **not** reconfigured: the DATASET_UPDATE saga re-applies the same protected route and the FROST project stays private. Anonymous read access is granted by **OPA**, which re-reads the now-`true` flag from the AuthZ Repository on the next request (after its short attribute-cache TTL) — there is no FROST `public` flag and no auth-plugin removal anymore. `assignments` and `namedApis` are omitted so the null reconciler leaves them untouched (keeps step 10 green; named APIs are immutable while released anyway).

  **Precondition:** CREATE saga (step 8) has settled (`pendingSagaType == null`, polled in pre-request); dataset is AVAILABLE.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, body `openDataAccess: true`. The route stays protected; OPA then grants anonymous payload reads once it re-reads the flag (verified in 9g).
}
